<p>&nbsp;A <a href="https://www.buckydrop.com/?ref=blog.buckydrop.com" rel="noreferrer"><u>China sourcing agent</u></a>&nbsp;should make the supplier-side workflow visible enough for a seller to understand where money and time are being added. The goal is not merely to find a lower product price; it is to turn the product into a trackable, deliverable US order.</p><h2 id="2-a-usd-example-why-the-product-price-is-not-the-order-cost"><strong>2. A USD Example: Why the Product Price Is Not the Order Cost</strong></h2><p>Consider a hypothetical Shopify product sold for <strong>$34.99</strong>. The figures below are illustrative only; they are not BuckyDrop quotes or promised rates.</p>
