font-size:10.0000pt;">Practical test:</span></b><span style="font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:'Noto Sans CJK SC';mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
line-height:120%;color:rgb(23,54,93);mso-ansi-font-weight:normal;
font-size:10.0000pt;"><span style="mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span>Run three versions for the same SKU: expected parcel data, a heavier parcel, and a remote US ZIP code. If the offer is profitable only in the best-case version, the product is not ready for paid traffic.</span><span style="font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:'Noto Sans CJK SC';mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
color:rgb(36,52,71);font-size:10.5000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<h2 id="3-what-most-often-destroys-margin-on-us-orders"><strong>3. What Most Often Destroys Margin on US Orders?</strong></h2><h3 id="dimensional-weight"><strong>Dimensional weight</strong></h3><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card"><img src="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/package2.jpg" class="kg-image" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1254" height="837" srcset="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w600/2026/09/package2.jpg 600w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w1000/2026/09/package2.jpg 1000w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/package2.jpg 1254w" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 720px"></figure><p>Carriers may charge by billable weight rather than scale weight. Bulky but light products—pillows, large organizers, plush goods or oversized packaging—can therefore cost more to ship than expected. Record the packed dimensions, not only the product dimensions.</p><h3 id="several-suppliers-for-one-customer-order"><strong>Several suppliers for one customer order</strong></h3><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card"><img src="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/Dropshipping-Product.jpg" class="kg-image" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1254" height="837" srcset="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w600/2026/09/Dropshipping-Product.jpg 600w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w1000/2026/09/Dropshipping-Product.jpg 1000w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/Dropshipping-Product.jpg 1254w" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 720px"></figure><p>If a customer purchases items sourced from different Chinese suppliers, the order may create several domestic shipments before consolidation. Consolidation can simplify the customer parcel, but it adds receiving time and must be compared with split-shipping cost and customer experience.</p><h3 id="variant-and-inventory-errors"><strong>Variant and inventory errors</strong></h3><p>A low-cost quote is meaningless if the wrong color, size or variant is purchased. Variant mapping, inventory updates and product-source binding matter because a replacement or refund can erase the margin from several successful orders.</p><h3 id="weak-packaging-decisions"><strong>Weak packaging decisions</strong></h3><p>Overpacking increases dimensional weight; underpacking increases damage risk. The best choice is product-specific. Fragile items, liquids, apparel and products with retail boxes need different handling rules.</p><h3 id="ignoring-failed-delivery-and-return-costs"><strong>Ignoring failed-delivery and return costs</strong></h3><p>US return expectations can be expensive for cross-border sellers. Before advertising, decide what happens when an address is wrong, a parcel is refused, tracking stops, or the customer requests a return. The policy shown in the store should match the workflow the business can actually support.</p><h2 id="4-how-long-does-dropshipping-shipping-to-the-us-take"><strong>4. How Long Does Dropshipping Shipping to the US Take?</strong></h2><p>Do not confuse carrier transit time with the customer’s total wait. For <a href="https://www.buckydrop.com/en/fee-calculator/?ref=blog.buckydrop.com"><u>international shipping from China to USA</u></a>, the complete timeline is:</p>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
