<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<p>&nbsp;There is no universally best model. Direct China fulfillment often makes sense while demand is uncertain. Local US inventory can make sense after a SKU has stable sales, predictable returns and enough margin to carry stock. A hybrid approach keeps the testing catalog flexible while placing proven items closer to customers through a separately arranged US warehouse.</p><p>At BuckyDrop, our strongest value is connecting China-side sourcing and <a href="https://www.buckydrop.com/?ref=blog.buckydrop.com" rel="noreferrer"><u>dropshipping fulfillment</u></a>&nbsp;in one operating workflow. Sellers can use that visibility to test products before making larger inventory commitments.</p><h2 id="6-us-import-charges-and-sales-tax-two-different-questions"><strong>6. US Import Charges and Sales Tax: Two Different Questions</strong></h2>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
