font-size:10.0000pt;">Important:</span></b><span style="font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:'Noto Sans CJK SC';mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
line-height:120%;color:rgb(23,54,93);mso-ansi-font-weight:normal;
font-size:10.0000pt;"><span style="mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span>This section is operational guidance, not legal or tax advice. Rules depend on product, origin, value, importer arrangement, destination, sales activity and current law. Verify with CBP, state authorities and qualified advisors.</span><span style="font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:'Noto Sans CJK SC';mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
color:rgb(36,52,71);font-size:10.5000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<h3 id="import-duties-and-customs"><strong>Import duties and customs</strong></h3><p>Do not build a 2026 US pricing model on the assumption that every shipment under $800 is duty-free. US Customs and Border Protection states that duty-free de minimis treatment was suspended for qualifying low-value imports from all countries effective August 29, 2025. Applicable duties, taxes and fees can therefore affect the delivered cost. Product classification, declared value, country of origin, carrier method and importer arrangement matter.</p><h3 id="us-sales-tax"><strong>US sales tax</strong></h3><p>Sales tax is separate from import duty. Shopify explains that US tax liability can depend on where products ship from and to, where the seller is registered, product taxability, buyer exemptions, and physical or economic nexus. Inventory or fulfillment activity in a state can affect the analysis. Determine where the business is required to register before enabling collection; BuckyDrop does not determine or file a seller’s US tax obligations.</p><h3 id="product-and-platform-requirements"><strong>Product and platform requirements</strong></h3><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card"><img src="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/Pros-and-Cons4.jpg" class="kg-image" alt="" loading="lazy" width="1218" height="861" srcset="https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w600/2026/09/Pros-and-Cons4.jpg 600w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/size/w1000/2026/09/Pros-and-Cons4.jpg 1000w, https://blog.buckydrop.com/content/images/2026/09/Pros-and-Cons4.jpg 1218w" sizes="(min-width: 720px) 720px"></figure><p>Before listing a product, confirm whether it is restricted for import, needs testing or labeling, contains batteries, liquids, magnets, branded intellectual property or other controlled characteristics, and is permitted by the payment provider and ecommerce platform. Accurate descriptions, values and product data help prevent avoidable customs and customer-service problems.</p><p>·&nbsp;Confirm the product category, materials, battery/liquid/magnet status and brand authorization.</p><p>·&nbsp;Confirm who is responsible for import declarations, duties and exception handling under the selected route.</p><p>·&nbsp;Review sales-tax nexus with state authorities or a qualified professional.</p><p>·&nbsp;Set a store policy for delivery estimates, address changes, failed delivery, refunds and returns.</p><h2 id="7-shopify-settings-that-affect-fulfillment-cost-and-customer-trust"><strong>7. Shopify Settings That Affect Fulfillment Cost and Customer Trust</strong></h2><p>A <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/buckydrop?ref=blog.buckydrop.com"><u>Shopify dropshipping fulfillment</u></a>&nbsp;workflow is not complete when a parcel leaves the warehouse. Store settings must reflect the actual shipping operation.</p><p>·&nbsp;<strong>Product data:</strong>&nbsp;Keep SKU and variant mapping accurate; enter realistic weight and package data where the checkout setup uses them.</p><p>·&nbsp;<strong>Shipping rates:</strong>&nbsp;Decide whether to charge a flat rate, calculated rate or free shipping built into the product price. Protect margin for oversized or remote-destination orders.</p><p>·&nbsp;<strong>Fulfillment location:</strong>&nbsp;Understand how Shopify assigns inventory and routes orders when more than one location or service is configured.</p><p>·&nbsp;<strong>Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure the carrier or tracking URL is returned to the order so customers can use Shopify’s order-status page and shipping notifications.</p><p>·&nbsp;<strong>Delivery communication:</strong>&nbsp;Show a realistic processing window and transit estimate. Do not display a domestic-style promise for a cross-border workflow unless performance supports it.</p><p>The same operating questions apply to <u>WooCommerce dropshipping</u>: how orders reach the fulfillment workflow, how variants and sources are mapped, how inventory changes are synchronized and how tracking returns to the store.</p><h2 id="8-what-should-us-sellers-compare-in-a-dropshipping-fulfillment-platform"><strong>8. What Should US Sellers Compare in a Dropshipping Fulfillment Platform?</strong></h2><p>The <a href="https://www.buckydrop.com/?ref=blog.buckydrop.com"><u>best dropshipping fulfillment platform for Shopify</u></a> is not automatically the one with the lowest visible shipping number. It is the platform that makes the complete workflow testable for the seller’s product, destination and order volume.</p>
